atlas provider
# Harvested run6/run7 provider topology. ProviderStateFold already folds provider
# events; these are the resolution/placement/parity graphs above it, still to build.

architecture provider-graph
  consumes CapabilityBid
  consumes ArtifactParity
  canonical_name ProviderGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Resolution
  layer provider
  semantic_question Which providers can realize this capability, at what multidimensional metric?
  purpose Capability bids, tournament, fallback tree -- native/frappe/replicated/signal/sidecar/external/commercial/capacity/model/device/human bids scored on a vector (cost/quality/latency/trust/authority/locality/semantic-loss/availability), no scalar collapse. Anycast over equivalent realizations.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreProviderFrontier/tools/refresh_providers.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreProviderFrontier/provider-refresh.cue
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/provider_graphs.py.archive
  witness 2026-09-18 a provider refresh asked all 67 entries directly rather than reading any logged status: 12 answered as themselves with credentials this estate holds (cloudflare queues, workflows, pages, workers and kv; turso, render, vercel, github, firecrawl, posthog, sentry), 4 answered and refused the credential (cloudflare r2, d1, vectorize, workers-ai -- scope or not enabled, never absent), 24 hold no credential here and were not asked, 1 answered 400, and 26 are libraries or local runtimes that no endpoint can be asked about
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_provider_graphs.py.archive
  witness cmd/BonfyreProviderFrontier/tests/refresh_providers.test.mjs
  node_types CapabilityBid
  node_types ProviderTournament
  edge_types realizes
  edge_types falls_back_to
  forbidden_inference available -> authorized
  forbidden_inference cheapest -> valid
  interacts provider-state
  interacts address-plane
  interacts realization-measurement
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap ProviderStateFold folds events, the route-set daemon advertises/withdraws routes
  known_gap only ArchitectureLookup has real bids; every other capability still has an empty tournament, which is silence rather than a choice
  known_gap the Bun refresh replaces only reachability probes; it does not implement provider bidding or placement, and unconfigured endpoints remain not_probeable even with a credential

architecture placement-graph
  canonical_name PlacementGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Placement
  layer provider
  semantic_question Where does this run or reside, given locality and resource constraints?
  purpose The material placement of a selected realization across Mac fabric, LAN, GPU, device, remote. Distinct from ProviderGraph (who can) and RuntimeMesh (what instances exist).
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/provider_graphs.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_provider_graphs.py.archive
  node_types PlacementNode
  edge_types placed_on
  forbidden_inference placeable -> authorized to execute there
  interacts address-plane
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap CID prefix routing gives placement partitions over content digests
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture runtime-parity-graph
  canonical_name RuntimeParityGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Parity
  layer provider
  semantic_question Do direct, MCP, and HTTP carriers produce the same semantic result?
  purpose Proven semantic equivalence across execution carriers, so route selection can treat them as an equal-cost multipath group.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/provider_graphs.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_provider_graphs.py.archive
  node_types Carrier
  edge_types parity_with
  forbidden_inference a carrier ran -> semantic parity with the others
  interacts transport-phenotype
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap TransportPhenotype proved identical digest across direct/MCP already
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture realization-measurement
  owns RealizationCost
  consumes AtlasAnswer
  publishes CapabilityBid
  publishes ArtifactParity
  derived RealizationCost
  canonical_name RealizationMeasurement
  family provider
  domain Provider / Realization
  layer provider
  semantic_question What does each realization of this capability actually spend, measured rather than assumed?
  purpose ProviderGraph was implemented and witnessed but never fed -- provider_bids did not exist in the live control plane, so no capability had a competing realization and every request fell through to the most expensive carrier by default. This runs each rung of the cheapest-sufficient ladder (native / local / agent / external / human) against one real capability and records what it spent, in the unit that is actually scarce: context bytes delivered per answered question.
  maturity implemented
  # Demoted: every witness this carried was archived. The evidence was
  # retired and the claim was never revisited, which is the laundering the
  # atlas forbids -- reclaiming measured needs a witness that runs today.
  known_gap realization-measurement lost its live witness to archival and holds implemented until one runs again
  node_types Realization
  node_types LadderRung
  edge_types measures
  edge_types bids_for
  internal_calculus executed measurement (paths are run, not estimated)
  internal_calculus answer-digest comparison for artifact parity
  invariant a bid records real units; polarity belongs to the metric dimension, never to the caller's weights
  invariant a realization that was not executed does not bid
  forbidden_inference measured cheapest -> selected (authority and proof still admit)
  forbidden_inference byte-identical answers -> one provider (artifact identity and producer identity are orthogonal proof dimensions)
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/realization_measure.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_realization_measure.py.archive
  interacts provider-graph
  interacts atlas-context-provider
  source_lineage run8 provider-context-pressure
  source_lineage external chatgpt trajectory -- artifact vs producer identity orthogonality (Bernstein trusted-producer work)
  known_gap only ArchitectureLookup is measured; the native rung has no bidder yet for this capability

architecture physical-derivation
  canonical_name PhysicalDerivation
  family provider
  domain Provider / Physical Derivation
  layer provider/realization
  semantic_question What source, toolchain, environment names, bodies and observations physically realized this semantic demand?
  purpose Wraps ExecutionEnvironmentGraph and RealizationMeasurement with RealizationManifest, PhysicalExecutionFrame, RealizationObservation, ProviderModelUsageObservation, PhysicalDerivationReceipt, ProviderMaterializationReceipt and BodyAvailability identities. Provider receipts may expose token, cache, retry, wall-time or local CPU/GPU/VRAM dimensions without forcing absent dimensions to zero. A provider file, vector store, collection, container or batch object is replaceable physical residency of a Bonfyre representation rather than another artifact owner.
  maturity implemented
  owns RealizationManifest
  owns PhysicalExecutionFrame
  owns RealizationObservation
  owns ProviderModelUsageObservation
  owns PhysicalDerivationReceipt
  owns ProviderMaterializationReceipt
  owns BodyAvailability
  consumes CapabilityEnvironment
  consumes ResourceWeather
  consumes CapabilityBid
  publishes UsageOccurrence
  publishes PhysicalDerivationReceipt
  node_types RealizationManifest
  node_types PhysicalExecutionFrame
  node_types PhysicalDerivationReceipt
  node_types ProviderModelUsageObservation
  edge_types realizes
  edge_types materializes
  edge_types reuses_body
  invariant environment evidence records dependency names and references, never secret values
  invariant body reuse is keyed by derivation identity and current validity
  invariant a CURRENT BodyAvailability entry is admitted only after the named local body reads back to its declared SHA-256 digest; a different body cannot rebind the same derivation and representation identity, and invalidation withdraws reuse eligibility without erasing the historical body or receipt
  invariant an external provider reference may be reused only for the same provider, scoped representation digest and active materialization; it cannot be rebound to another body
  invariant releasing or expiry of a provider materialization records loss of reusable external residency and never deletes a canonical artifact, receipt, provider account or authority record
  invariant sparse provider usage remains explicit rather than becoming zero usage or billing truth
  invariant Codex aggregate usage may inherit route identity and an explicitly selected model from its immutable epoch launcher, but never infers a model from a CLI default
  invariant terminal epoch compaction preserves command argv only with its canonical digest; invalid compacted metadata cannot enrich usage coordinates
  invariant a carrier adapter binds every UsageOccurrence to stable attempt, realization, and physical-receipt identities
  invariant a pre-attempt-table usage row gains an attempt identity only when a retained carrier receipt exactly matches every stored usage and detail coordinate; a usage-only legacy row remains refused
  invariant carrier-declared attempt or realization identities cannot be rebound by an adapter
  forbidden_inference a command exited zero -> its semantic target is proven
  forbidden_inference a body digest -> producer identity or authority
  forbidden_inference provider file/vector-store/collection/container/batch identifier -> artifact identity, canonical knowledge, credential, authority, provider admission, output admission or effect right
  interacts physical-derivation-feeds-finance
  interacts terminal-epoch-receipt-feeds-finance
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/financial_metabolism.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/physical_derivation.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreProvider/src/main.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_physical_derivation.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_financial_metabolism.py.archive
  witness cmd/BonfyreProvider/tests/smoke.sh proves provider residency is deduplicated only by scoped representation identity, rejects opaque-reference rebinding, excludes release from reusable listings, and retains no credential/body
  witness cmd/BonfyreProvider/tests/smoke.sh proves BodyAvailability rejects a derivation/representation rebinding to different bytes, detects a later local-body mismatch, and makes a body unavailable after explicit invalidation
  witness 2026-09-24 the frozen 2,424-coordinate SourceFrontier static RuntimeImage closure was digested as f687126fd4fc2db941d99038e36466103a6d3ee0b131406d2013981e99fb3c74 and recorded CURRENT only after local readback; this proves physical closure availability, not source liveness, semantic success, authority, or effect completion
  source_lineage Run8 realization measurement and Generation-10 physical derivation ABI
